      "body": "### Neovim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.8.1\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nVim doesn't use the Lua API\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS 12.6.2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\niTerm2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\n3.5.0beta8\n\n### Installation\n\nHomebrew\n\n### How to reproduce the issue\n\n- Install neodev and set up neovim for plugin development such that sumneko_lua linters are linting your lua files\r\n- When calling `vim.fn.getline(\".\")`, note that you get a linter error telling you that the function only accepts `number`.\r\n- Read the documentation. Documentation says:\r\n\r\n```\r\n-- When {lnum} is a String that doesn't start with a\r\n-- digit, |line()| is called to translate the String into a Number.\r\n-- To get the line under the cursor: \r\n-- ```vim\r\n--   getline(\".\")\r\n-- ```\r\n```\r\n\r\n- From this, I infer that passing the string `\".\"` should be valid, but the linter does not agree (because it is referencing the documentation).\r\n\r\nPlease update the docstrings such that `string` is an accepted value (or, better yet, create an alias that allows for any number and then a string whose value can only be `\".\"`)\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nLinter would accept `\".\"` as a valid value for `getline()`\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nLinter shows a warning saying that the type doesn't match what is stated in the documentation.",
